# Custom lib — app/src/lib/text.ts fixed API

## Context

`app/src/lib/text.ts` is a CUSTOM library, NOT lodash/underscore. Its entire
supported surface is exactly three functions. Agents often hallucinate helpers
that do not exist here.

## Rule

- The current supported surface is exactly these three functions, with exactly
  these signatures:
  - `slugify(input: string): string`
  - `truncate(input: string, maxLength: number, suffix?: string): string`
  - `normalizeSpaces(input: string): string`
- NEVER call or import helpers that do not exist here (e.g. `capitalize`,
  `camelCase`, `deburr`, `kebabCase`, `startCase`, `escape`).
- NEVER assume a lodash/underscore-style API. Additional helpers are allowed
  ONLY when added as named exports in `app/src/lib/text.ts` with a colocated
  test — do not invent or import an unimplemented helper.
- Do not change the existing three signatures; only add new named exports.

## How to verify

1. `grep -rn "from \"./lib/text" app/src` (and `.js`) only references
   `slugify` / `truncate` / `normalizeSpaces`, or a helper actually defined in
   `text.ts`.
2. `cd app && npm run typecheck` passes (a hallucinated import would fail here).
3. `app/src/lib/text.ts` still exports exactly the three original functions
   (plus any you deliberately added).




